    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`build_client` is implemented in `app/llm_client.py` and meets all four requirements. The test suite passes (1 test), and I checked the behaviour with a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500.\n\n**Note:** the pinned openai 3.19.2 uses **`httpx2`** as its HTTP library, not `httpx`, and `httpx` isn't installed. `OpenAI(http_client=...)` expects an `httpx2.Client`, so the code imports `httpx2`. It's already installed as a dependency of openai, so nothing new was added. Any stub transport your tests pass in must also be an `httpx2` transport, such as `httpx2.MockTransport`.\n\nHow it works:\n- **Timeouts:** `httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)`, set on both the HTTP client and `OpenAI(timeout=...)`. The SDK sends a timeout with every request, so setting it only on the HTTP client wouldn't be enough.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** a request event hook logs `\"%s %s\"` (method, URL) at INFO level on the `app.http` logger. The SDK sends every retry through the same HTTP client, so retries are logged too.\n- **Transport:** passed to `openai.DefaultHttpxClient`. That class keeps the SDK's default connection limits and redirect behaviour, which a plain `httpx2.Client` would drop.\n\n**Check results:** one `models.list()` call made 3 requests (the first try plus 2 retries). Each produced its own `app.http INFO GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` line and carried the timeout `connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0`.\n\nOne cleanup item: the check script `_check.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed permission. You can delete it, or tell me to."
  },
